## 13. Definition of Done

The work is complete only when:

1. The existing application has been upgraded rather than replaced with an unrelated demo.
2. The pages follow one distinctive and cohesive visual identity.
3. The result avoids the generic AI dashboard aesthetic described above.
4. All implemented pages work across desktop, tablet, and mobile.
5. Existing backend APIs and authentication are integrated correctly.
6. Issue submission and other supported actions persist through the real backend.
7. Data displayed in the interface comes from actual API responses or is clearly identified as an empty state.
8. Forms have proper validation and useful feedback.
9. Loading, error, success, and empty states have been designed.
10. Accessibility and keyboard navigation have been considered throughout.
11. No working backend functionality, authentication, or existing data has been unnecessarily removed.
12. The application passes the available type checks, linting, and production build.

